## For AI Agents

This CLI is designed for AI Agent consumption. Key usage patterns:

### General calling pattern

```bash
# Query a list (GET with query params)
{{PROJECT_NAME}}-api-cli <module> get <path> --params='{"page":1,"pageSize":20}'

# Get a single record by ID (GET with path params)
{{PROJECT_NAME}}-api-cli <module> get <path>/:id --path-params='{"id":"123"}'

# Create a record (POST with body)
{{PROJECT_NAME}}-api-cli <module> post <path> --params='{"field":"value"}'

# Update a record (PUT with path params + body)
{{PROJECT_NAME}}-api-cli <module> put <path>/:id --path-params='{"id":"123"}' --params='{"field":"newValue"}'

# Partial update (PATCH with path params + body)
{{PROJECT_NAME}}-api-cli <module> patch <path>/:id --path-params='{"id":"123"}' --params='{"field":"newValue"}'

# Delete a record (DELETE with path params)
{{PROJECT_NAME}}-api-cli <module> delete <path>/:id --path-params='{"id":"123"}'
```

### Auth configuration

For authenticated APIs, set the token once in config rather than passing `--headers` every time:

```bash
cat > {{PROJECT_NAME}}-api-cli/config.json << 'EOF'
{
  "baseUrl": "{{BASE_URL}}",
  "headers": { "Authorization": "Bearer <token>" },
  "timeout": 30000
}
EOF
```

Or use the built-in auth commands:

```bash
{{PROJECT_NAME}}-api-cli auth login --token <bearer-token>
{{PROJECT_NAME}}-api-cli auth login --cookie "session=abc; csrf=xyz"
{{PROJECT_NAME}}-api-cli auth status --json
{{PROJECT_NAME}}-api-cli auth logout
```

### Output format

All commands output JSON to stdout by default. Errors are written to stderr as:
```json
{ "error": true, "status": 401, "data": { "message": "Unauthorized" } }
```

Exit code is `1` on error, `0` on success.

Use `--output=table` for human-readable table format, `--output=raw` for raw text.

### Override base URL per request

```bash
{{PROJECT_NAME}}-api-cli <module> get <path> --base-url='http://staging.example.com:3000'
```

### Override auth header per request

```bash
{{PROJECT_NAME}}-api-cli <module> get <path> --headers='{"Authorization":"Bearer <other-token>"}'
```

